LOCAL1="FlightGear's Timezone folder is a link into the system's time zone files"
LOCAL2="%s is a link to %s, left behind by an old Debian FlightGear data package. Removing or replacing FlightGear's data goes through that link and deletes the system's time zone files, and %s of them were already overwritten by FlightGear's copies. Repair removes the link and reinstalls the time zone packages (and Debian's flightgear-data-base, if it is installed) from the package archive, which needs the network."
LOCAL3="%s is a link to %s, and %s of the system's time zone files are missing: the clock shows UTC and programs say the time zone is not installed. Repair removes the link and reinstalls the time zone packages from the package archive, which needs the network. Repair also finishes the installation of FlightGear's data that was waiting, a download of about 1.75 GiB."
